### Business rules

- Search/filter/sort operate on actual catalog records. Sanitize search terms and constrain page size.
- Counts are derived from real published records, except separately labelled reference metadata.
- Favorites are idempotent and owner-scoped.
- Preset actions resolve a catalog item, check support status, active connection, host capabilities, selection requirements and user permission before creating an operation job.
- Every AE job includes a validated operation name and typed parameters, never arbitrary cloud-supplied JSX or executable source.
- A job has a state machine and valid transitions. Duplicate job result submissions must not execute the operation twice.
- Failed operations return a human-readable safe message plus a stable error code and a correlation/request ID.
- Retry only when the operation is safe and idempotent, or after explicit user confirmation.
- Project file metadata is distinct from an uploaded file. A local file path is not portable cloud storage.
- For caption and downloader jobs, report only progress emitted by the actual local process. Respect cancel/timeout and clean temporary files safely.
- Catalog publish/unpublish and asset deletion should be auditable. Keep a revision/rollback path for catalog edits.
- Do not allow the admin UI to mutate arbitrary server environment variables or secret values.

